## 3. STRICT UDN BUSINESS RULE

The University of Da Nang includes eight configured member institutions:

- DUT.
- DUE.
- UED.
- UFL.
- UTE.
- VKU.
- VNUK.
- SMP.

All eight share:

`schoolReviewUnitId = unit-udn`

There is one shared School reviewer account.

The original institution of each Student must remain unchanged.

### Batch scope

The batch belongs to the School Review Unit, NOT to the individual member institution.

The UDN reviewer can filter the application list by member institution.

However, filtering to DUT or DUE must never create a separate forwarding batch.

The underlying batch always covers the same UDN review unit and season.

### Expected result

One UDN list containing selected applications from any of the eight member institutions.

One common official decision document.

One final submission.

After successful submission, the UDN reviewer cannot normally forward additional applications for that season.

Independent non-UDN School Review Units have their own separate seasonal batches.

Do not create eight member-school reviewer accounts or eight UDN forwarding batches.

